---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const toc = [
  ['install', 'Install'], ['html', 'Plain HTML / any framework'], ['react', 'React'], ['vue', 'Vue'], ['angular', 'Angular, Svelte, Solid'], ['vanilla', 'Vanilla JS API'],
  ['options', 'Options'], ['content', 'Content: HTML, Markdown, JSON'], ['rendering', 'Rendering content anywhere'], ['uploads', 'Images & uploads'],
  ['ai', 'AI'], ['theming', 'Theming & dark mode'], ['extensions', 'Extensions & custom menus'], ['shortcuts', 'Keyboard shortcuts'],
]
const c = (s: string) => s
---
<Base title="Docs — Penna">
  <div class="wrap docs">
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      {toc.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}
    </nav>
    <article>
      <h1>Documentation</h1>
      <p class="lead">Penna is a headless-when-you-want, batteries-included-when-you-don't editor built on ProseMirror. Five packages, all MIT:</p>
      <table class="pk">
        <tr><td><code>@abhinavakhil/penna-core</code></td><td>The editor, its UI, commands, Markdown/HTML/JSON I/O, <code>renderToHTML</code>, and <code>penna.css</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@abhinavakhil/penna-element</code></td><td><code>&lt;penna-editor&gt;</code> web component. Use it from Angular, Svelte, Solid, Lit, HTMX, plain HTML.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@abhinavakhil/penna-react</code></td><td><code>&lt;Penna&gt;</code>, <code>usePenna()</code>, <code>usePennaState()</code>, <code>&lt;PennaContent&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@abhinavakhil/penna-vue</code></td><td>Same for Vue 3, with <code>v-model</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@abhinavakhil/penna-ai</code></td><td>AI extension: free providers, streaming, accept/discard UI.</td></tr>
      </table>

      <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
      <pre class="code">npm i @abhinavakhil/penna-core            <span class="c"># always</span>
npm i @abhinavakhil/penna-react           <span class="c"># or @abhinavakhil/penna-vue, or @abhinavakhil/penna-element</span>
npm i @abhinavakhil/penna-ai              <span class="c"># optional</span></pre>
      <p>Import the stylesheet once, anywhere: <code>import '@abhinavakhil/penna-core/penna.css'</code>. It styles the editor <em>and</em> rendered content.</p>

      <h2 id="html">Plain HTML / any framework</h2>
      <p>The web component needs no build step and works everywhere custom elements do (every modern browser, every framework).</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/@abhinavakhil/penna-core/dist/penna.css"&gt;
&lt;script type="module" src="https://unpkg.com/@abhinavakhil/penna-element"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;penna-editor id="ed" placeholder="Write…" theme="auto" autosave-key="draft"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Initial &lt;strong&gt;HTML&lt;/strong&gt; can go right here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/penna-editor&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
  const ed = document.getElementById('ed')
  ed.addEventListener('change', (e) =&gt; console.log(e.detail.html, e.detail.json, e.detail.markdown))
  ed.value = '&lt;p&gt;set content&lt;/p&gt;'     // get/set in the element's format (html | markdown | json)
  ed.editor                          // the full PennaEditor instance
  ed.options = { onUpload, extensions: [ai({...})] }   // set before it's attached
&lt;/script&gt;`)}></pre>
      <p>Attributes: <code>value</code>, <code>placeholder</code>, <code>readonly</code>, <code>theme</code>, <code>format</code> (html | markdown | json), <code>toolbar="false"</code>, <code>autosave-key</code>. Events: <code>change</code>, <code>ready</code>, <code>editor-focus</code>, <code>editor-blur</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="react">React</h2>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`import { Penna, usePenna, usePennaState, PennaContent } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-react'
import { ai } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-ai'
import '@abhinavakhil/penna-core/penna.css'

function Editor() {
  const [doc, setDoc] = useState(null)          // store JSON (recommended) or html/markdown
  const ref = useRef(null)                        // PennaEditor instance
  return (
    &lt;Penna
      ref={ref}
      defaultValue={doc}
      placeholder="Write something…"
      onChange={({ json, html, markdown }) =&gt; setDoc(json)}
      onUpload={async (file) =&gt; (await upload(file)).url}
      extensions={[ai({ provider: 'groq', apiKey: KEY })]}
    /&gt;
  )
}

// A custom toolbar rendered inside &lt;Penna&gt; children can use the context:
function WordCount() {
  const editor = usePenna()
  const count = usePennaState(editor, (e) =&gt; e.wordCount())
  return &lt;span&gt;{count?.words} words&lt;/span&gt;
}

// Display saved content without loading the editor (works in server components too):
&lt;PennaContent json={doc} /&gt;`)}></pre>
      <p><code>value</code> makes it controlled (external changes reset the doc; your own edits don't). <code>defaultValue</code> is uncontrolled. Both accept HTML, Markdown (with <code>contentFormat="markdown"</code>) or JSON.</p>

      <h2 id="vue">Vue</h2>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`&lt;script setup&gt;
import { Penna, PennaContent } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-vue'
import { ai } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-ai'
import '@abhinavakhil/penna-core/penna.css'
const doc = ref(null)
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;Penna v-model="doc" format="json" placeholder="Write…" :options="{ extensions: [ai({ provider: 'groq', apiKey })] }" /&gt;
  &lt;PennaContent :json="doc" /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;`)}></pre>

      <h2 id="angular">Angular, Svelte, Solid, Lit…</h2>
      <p>Use <code>@abhinavakhil/penna-element</code>. Import it once (e.g. in <code>main.ts</code>), then use the tag. Angular needs <code>CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA</code> on the module/component.</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`// Angular
&lt;penna-editor [value]="html" (change)="html = $event.detail.html" placeholder="Write…"&gt;&lt;/penna-editor&gt;

// Svelte
&lt;penna-editor value={html} on:change={(e) =&gt; (html = e.detail.html)} /&gt;

// Solid
&lt;penna-editor prop:value={html()} on:change={(e) =&gt; setHtml(e.detail.html)} /&gt;`)}></pre>

      <h2 id="vanilla">Vanilla JS API</h2>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`import { createEditor } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-core'

const editor = createEditor('#editor', { placeholder: 'Write…' })

editor.getJSON() / editor.getHTML() / editor.getMarkdown() / editor.getText()
editor.setJSON(json) / editor.setHTML(html) / editor.setMarkdown(md)
editor.insertContent('&lt;p&gt;hi&lt;/p&gt;')            // at the cursor
editor.readonly = true                          // toggle read-only
editor.theme = 'dark'                           // 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto'
editor.focus() / editor.isEmpty() / editor.wordCount()
editor.exec(editor.commands.heading(2))         // run any command
editor.exec(editor.commands.image('https://…'))
editor.exec(editor.commands.table(3, 3))
editor.on('update', (e) =&gt; save(e.getJSON()))  // 'update' | 'selection' | 'focus' | 'blur'
editor.toggleFind() / editor.openLinkEditor()
editor.destroy()`)}></pre>
      <p>Every command in <code>editor.commands</code> is a plain ProseMirror command, so anything from the ProseMirror ecosystem works with <code>editor.view</code> and <code>editor.state</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="options">Options</h2>
      <table class="opts">
        <tr><td><code>content</code></td><td>Initial content: HTML string, Markdown string (set <code>contentFormat: 'markdown'</code>) or JSON doc.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td>Empty-document hint. Empty lines show "Type '/' for commands".</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>readonly</code></td><td>Start read-only. Toggle later with <code>editor.readonly</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>theme</code></td><td><code>'auto'</code> (default, follows system), <code>'light'</code>, <code>'dark'</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>toolbar</code></td><td><code>false</code> to hide the fixed toolbar, or an array of items to customise it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>bubbleMenu</code> / <code>slashMenu</code></td><td><code>false</code> to disable, or an array of items.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dragHandle</code> / <code>statusBar</code></td><td><code>false</code> to disable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>borderless</code></td><td>No border or focus ring. Nice inside your own card.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>typography</code></td><td>Configure heading/body defaults and the font family, size, and line-height choices shown in the toolbar.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>onUpload(file)</code></td><td>Return a URL for a dropped/pasted/picked file. Default: inline data URL.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>autosave</code></td><td><code>{'{ key, storage?, debounceMs? }'}</code>. Restores on mount. <code>editor.clearAutosave()</code> to reset.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>extensions</code></td><td>Array of extensions such as <code>ai()</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>onUpdate</code>, <code>onSelectionChange</code>, <code>onFocus</code>, <code>onBlur</code></td><td>Callbacks with the editor instance.</td></tr>
      </table>

      <h2 id="content">Content: HTML, Markdown, JSON</h2>
      <p><b>JSON is canonical</b> and lossless. HTML is lossless for everything Penna can produce. Markdown covers everything but colors/alignment (rendered as plain text). Recommended: store JSON, render with <code>renderToHTML</code>.</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`import { renderToHTML, toMarkdown, fromMarkdown } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-core'
renderToHTML(json)            // string, no DOM needed
toMarkdown(fromMarkdown(md))  // parser/serializer are exported too`)}></pre>

      <h2 id="rendering">Rendering content anywhere</h2>
      <p>Three ways to show saved content:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Server / no editor:</b> <code>renderToHTML(json)</code> and wrap it in <code>&lt;div class="penna-content"&gt;</code> with <code>penna.css</code> loaded. Pixel-identical to the editor. Works in Node, Workers, Deno, Bun.</li>
        <li><b>React / Vue:</b> <code>&lt;PennaContent json={"{doc}"} /&gt;</code>.</li>
        <li><b>Read-only editor:</b> <code>createEditor(el, {'{ content, readonly: true, toolbar: false }'})</code>. Checkbox and embed interactions still work.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Sanitise on the server if content comes from untrusted users. The schema already rejects <code>script</code>, inline handlers and unknown tags, but defence in depth is cheap.</p>

      <h2 id="uploads">Images & uploads</h2>
      <p>Drop, paste, pick from the toolbar, or <code>/image</code>. Images get resize handles, alignment and alt text when selected. Videos too. By default files are stored inline as data URLs so it works with zero setup; for real apps pass <code>onUpload</code>:</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`createEditor('#editor', {
  onUpload: async (file) =&gt; {
    const { url } = await supabase.storage.from('images').upload(\`\${crypto.randomUUID()}-\${file.name}\`, file)
    return url   // any string URL — S3, Cloudinary, your API…
  },
})`)}></pre>
      <p>Pasting a bare image URL inserts an image. Pasting a YouTube / Vimeo / Loom / Figma / CodePen link on an empty line inserts an embed. Pasting a URL over selected text makes a link.</p>

      <h2 id="ai">AI</h2>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`import { ai } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-ai'

createEditor('#editor', {
  extensions: [
    ai({
      provider: 'groq',          // 'groq' | 'gemini' | 'openrouter' | 'together' | 'ollama'
      apiKey: KEY,               //  | 'openai' | 'mistral' | 'openai-compatible'
      // model: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile',   // optional, each provider has a good default
      // baseUrl: 'https://your-proxy/v1',   // required for 'openai-compatible'
      // fetch: myFetch,                     // route through your server
      // actions: [...defaultActions, myAction],
    }),
  ],
})`)}></pre>
      <p><b>Free by default.</b> Groq, Gemini, OpenRouter and Together all have free tiers; Ollama is free and local. <b>Paid models</b> work through the OpenAI, Mistral presets or any OpenAI-compatible URL (Anthropic via a shim, Azure, Vercel AI Gateway, LiteLLM, your own proxy).</p>
      <p><b>Triggers:</b> <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>J</kbd>, the ✦ button in the bubble menu and toolbar, or <code>/ai</code> and <code>/continue</code>. Results stream into a preview; nothing changes the document until you accept.</p>
      <p><b>Custom actions:</b> an action is <code>{'{ id, title, prompt(ctx) → messages, mode?: "replace" | "insert", askInput? }'}</code>. Pass <code>actions</code> to replace the list, or spread <code>defaultActions</code> to extend it.</p>
      <p><b>Production note:</b> a key in the browser is visible to your users. Point <code>baseUrl</code> at a tiny proxy that adds the key server-side, or pass a custom <code>fetch</code>. Hosted Penna AI (no key, usage-billed) is planned; <code>provider: 'penna'</code> is reserved for it.</p>

      <h2 id="theming">Theming & dark mode</h2>
      <p>Dark mode follows <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> automatically. Force it with <code>theme: 'dark'</code> or <code>data-theme="dark"</code> on any ancestor (or the editor root). Every color is a CSS variable on <code>.penna</code> and <code>.penna-content</code>:</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`.penna, .penna-content {
  --pn-font: Inter, sans-serif;
  --pn-accent: #e11d48;        /* links, active buttons, selection */
  --pn-bg: #fff;  --pn-fg: #111;  --pn-muted: #666;  --pn-border: #eee;
  --pn-surface: #fff;          /* menus, toolbar */
  --pn-radius: 12px;
  --pn-highlight: #fef08a;  --pn-code-bg: #f3f4f6;  --pn-pre-bg: #0f172a;
}`)}></pre>
      <p>Class names are stable and prefixed with <code>pn-</code> if you want to go further.</p>
      <p>Typography choices are stored on paragraph and heading nodes, so JSON and HTML preserve them. Penna never downloads fonts in your users' applications; load the families you expose through your own CSS or font host:</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`createEditor('#editor', {
  typography: {
    bodyFontFamily: 'Inter',
    headingFontFamily: 'Plus Jakarta Sans',
    fontFamilies: [
      { label: 'Brand Sans', value: 'Brand Sans' },
      { label: 'Editorial Serif', value: 'Lora' },
    ],
    fontSizes: ['14px', '16px', '18px', '24px', '32px'],
    lineHeights: ['1', '1.25', '1.5', '1.75', '2'],
  },
})`)}></pre>

      <h2 id="extensions">Extensions & custom menus</h2>
      <p>An extension is a plain object. This is how <code>@abhinavakhil/penna-ai</code> is built, and it's enough for most needs:</p>
      <pre class="code" set:html={c(`import { commands, type PennaExtension } from '@abhinavakhil/penna-core'

const signature: PennaExtension = {
  name: 'signature',
  slashItems: [{ id: 'sig', title: 'Signature', icon: '✍️', group: 'Custom', run: (view) =&gt; {
    view.dispatch(view.state.tr.insertText('— Abhinav'))
  }}],
  bubbleItems: [{ id: 'shout', icon: 'highlight', label: 'Shout', run: (view) =&gt; commands.highlight('#fca5a5')(view.state, view.dispatch) }],
  toolbarItems: ['|', { id: 'sig', icon: 'text', label: 'Signature', run: (view) =&gt; view.dispatch(view.state.tr.insertText('— Abhinav')) }],
  plugins: (editor) =&gt; [ /* any ProseMirror plugins */ ],
}
createEditor('#editor', { extensions: [signature] })`)}></pre>
      <p>To fully replace a menu, pass your own array to <code>toolbar</code>, <code>bubbleMenu</code> or <code>slashMenu</code>. <code>defaultToolbarItems</code>, <code>defaultBubbleItems</code> and <code>defaultSlashItems</code> are exported so you can filter or reorder them. The schema, keymap, input rules and every plugin are exported from <code>@abhinavakhil/penna-core</code> if you want to build something entirely different on top.</p>

      <h2 id="shortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <table class="opts">
        <tr><td><kbd>/</kbd></td><td>Insert block menu</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> / <kbd>I</kbd> / <kbd>U</kbd> / <kbd>E</kbd></td><td>Bold / italic / underline / code</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd> / <kbd>H</kbd></td><td>Strikethrough / highlight</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd></td><td>Link</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>J</kbd></td><td>Ask AI</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>F</kbd></td><td>Find & replace</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>0-3</kbd></td><td>Paragraph / heading 1-3</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>7</kbd> / <kbd>8</kbd> / <kbd>9</kbd></td><td>Numbered / bullet / task list</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd></td><td>Quote, code block</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> / <kbd>E</kbd> / <kbd>R</kbd></td><td>Align left / center / right</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Indent / outdent list, next / previous table cell</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Exit code block · <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> line break</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>\</kbd></td><td>Clear formatting</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Markdown</td><td><code># </code> <code>- </code> <code>1. </code> <code>[ ] </code> <code>&gt; </code> <code>```</code> <code>---</code> <code>**bold**</code> <code>_italic_</code> <code>~~strike~~</code> <code>==mark==</code> <code>`code`</code></td></tr>
      </table>
    </article>
  </div>

  <style>
    .docs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 48px; padding: 40px 20px; align-items: start; }
    .toc { position: sticky; top: 80px; display: grid; gap: 2px; font-size: 13px; }
    .toc a { padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--muted); }
    .toc a:hover { background: var(--code); color: var(--fg); }
    article { min-width: 0; max-width: 760px; }
    article h1 { font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    article h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 48px 0 12px; padding-top: 8px; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
    article p, article li { font-size: 15px; }
    article code { background: var(--code); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; }
    article pre.code { margin: 12px 0 16px; }
    article pre.code code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: inherit; }
    .lead { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); }
    table.pk, table.opts { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; margin: 12px 0; }
    .pk td, .opts td { padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
    .pk td:first-child, .opts td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; width: 1%; }
    kbd { font-size: 11px; padding: 1px 5px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom-width: 2px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--card); }
    @media (max-width: 800px) { .docs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .toc { position: static; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  </style>
</Base>
